#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Scryer.cfg:27
msgid ""
"This unit can read the near future and tell allied units the weakness and "
"general stance of enemies entering combat.  Units that are next to it fight "
"better and ignore all enemy Zones of Control."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Scryer.cfg:110
msgid "desert wind"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Sentinel, race=phantom_egypt
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Sentinel.cfg:4
msgid "Tomb Sentinel"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Shade, race=phantom_egypt
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Shade.cfg:84
msgid "Vapor"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Shade, race=phantom_egypt
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Shade.cfg:92
msgid ""
"The Vapor can take the form of a real fighter, but the deception is apparent "
"when the opponent attacks and the vapor dissipates.\n"
"Special Note:  The phantom generated from this unit will die when struck by "
"an attacker, regardless of hitpoints."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Shield, race=phantom_egypt
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Shield.cfg:5
msgid "Tomb Shield-Guard"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Slave, race=phantom_egypt
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Slave.cfg:4
msgid "Holy Slave"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Slave, race=phantom_egypt
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Slave.cfg:18
msgid ""
"Holy Slaves are involuntary members of the ancient priesthood.  They do most "
"of the menial work at the temples, but they do receive some training for "
"recording and channeling the will of the gods and higher priests."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Stalker, race=phantom_egypt, gender=female
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Stalker.cfg:4
msgid "Stalker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Wing, race=phantom_egypt, gender=female
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Wing.cfg:4
msgid "Wing Dancer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Tomb Wing, race=phantom_egypt, gender=female
#: ./units/phantom/Tomb_Wing.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Higher priestesses of the strange sword-dance are fearsome warriors, but they"
" still have the same ability to feignt and distract the opponent so that they"
" can slip through gaps in enemy formations."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Cutter, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter.cfg:5
msgid "Cutter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Cutter, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter.cfg:25
msgid ""
"Primeval Cutters are not particularly strong, but they can launch cutting "
"metal discs. Cutters are able to provide a counter to enemy archers."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=ranged
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter.cfg:35
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Aerowheel.cfg:39
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Ironwheel.cfg:33
msgid "chakram"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Aerowheel, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Aerowheel.cfg:5
msgid "Aerowheel"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Aerowheel, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Aerowheel.cfg:27
msgid ""
"Having mastered the cutting wheel, a Primeval Ironwheel must make a choice "
"whether to focus on the disc weapon or to tend to other skills required of a "
"high ranking soldier. Primeval Aerowheels have chosen the latter and are "
"mixed fighters."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Firewheel, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Firewheel.cfg:5
msgid "Firewheel"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Firewheel, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Firewheel.cfg:43
msgid "Primeval Firewheels..."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=ranged
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Firewheel.cfg:56
msgid "firewheel"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Ironwheel, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Ironwheel.cfg:5
msgid "Ironwheel"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Ironwheel, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Ironwheel.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Primeval technology is a bit of a mystery. The Ironwheels are unusually "
"accurate with their cutting discs, and it is suspected that their headgear "
"has something to do with this."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Sunwheel, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Sunwheel.cfg:5
msgid "Sun-Wheel"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Sunwheel, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Sunwheel.cfg:32
msgid ""
"The name for the superior blade-throwers is 'Sun Wheel'.  Whether this is "
"because the sun is exhalted or just because it hurts the primeval eyes like a"
" seering blade is anyone's guess."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=blade, range=ranged
#: ./units/primeval/Cutter_Sunwheel.cfg:45
msgid "duosica"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Slow, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot.cfg:5
msgid "Slow Foot"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Slow, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot.cfg:20
msgid "A Slowfoot ..."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Giant, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Breaker.cfg:5
msgid "Line Breaker"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Giant, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Breaker.cfg:22
msgid ""
"The Primeval Line Breakers are very aggressive and strong, and use these "
"talents to punch a hole in enemy defensive formations.  Like the Drivers from"
" whose ranks they rose, they lead a rough and dangerous life.  But they "
"wouldn't have it any other way."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Breaker.cfg:33
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Driver.cfg:42
msgid "chain"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Dogface, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Dogface.cfg:5
msgid "Dogface"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Dogface, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Dogface.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Like the experienced chakram throwers, the Primeval soldiers wear some sort "
"of visor. Though it simply looks like a piece of metal strapped across the "
"eyes, the visor appears to assist the fighter in targeting the enemy."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Driver, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Driver.cfg:5
msgid "Driver"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Driver, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Driver.cfg:20
msgid ""
"Primeval Drivers are not that much smaller than a Troll. They have risen out "
"of the Slowfoot ranks through strength and experience. With enough luck and "
"determination, they might be able to escape their caste and join the ranks of"
" the Line Breakers."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Titan, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Titan.cfg:5
msgid "Titan"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Titan, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Titan.cfg:22
msgid ""
"The Primeval Titans are the most powerful wariors, some seemed destined to "
"join the Pantheon."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Warrior, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Warrior.cfg:5
msgid "Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Warrior, race=primeval
#: ./units/primeval/Foot_Warrior.cfg:20
msgid "The Primeval Warriors ..."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Celebrant, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Celebrant.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Celebrant"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Celebrant, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Celebrant.cfg:30
msgid ""
"Though their faith in the Primeval beings has not flagged, their faith in "
"their own ability to bring the necessary pain to the enemy has (some would "
"say these are the wisest of all the Primevalists). They have instead turned "
"their attention to supporting their more confident brothers and have pursued "
"basic healing knowledge."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=arcane, range=ranged
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Celebrant.cfg:54
msgid "condemnation"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Fanatic, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Fanatic.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Fanatic"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Fanatic, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Fanatic.cfg:21
msgid ""
"When blind devotion is combined with combat experience, a more valuable "
"figher is formed. They know enough to be dangerous, but not enough to be "
"reasoned with."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Fanatic.cfg:41
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Fighter.cfg:38
msgid "darts"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Fighter, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Fighter.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Fighter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Fighter, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Fighter.cfg:21
msgid ""
"The primevalists are mostly angry young men. The Dark Messiah told them what "
"they needed to hear to pick up a sword and attack their fellow humans in some"
" misguided attempt to please the Primevals. Upon joining the movement, each "
"fighter and follower is given a tattoo that is supposed to ward off evil "
"spirits."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Follower, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Follower.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Follower"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Follower, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Follower.cfg:28
msgid ""
"Some of the angry young men recruited by the Dark Messiah are more clever "
"than they are strong. These followers have some minimal magical training and "
"put it to use against their fellow humans in some misguided attempt to please"
" the Primevals. Upon joining the movement, each fighter and follower is given"
" a tattoo that is supposed to ward off evil spirits."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=cold, range=ranged
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Follower.cfg:47
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Monk.cfg:47
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Prior.cfg:58
#: ./units/south-seas/Caster.cfg:40
msgid "chill"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Leader, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Leader.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Leader"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Leader, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Leader.cfg:23
msgid ""
"While the Primevals most likely have as little respect for these warriors as "
"they do for any human, the other fanatics admire their dedication to the "
"(unfortunate) faith they all share.  Some of this admiration is due to a "
"unique ability:  Whether it is a gift granted by the Primeval Ones or just "
"the ability of a focused mind, no one can say - but the Leaders can cause a "
"piercing pain in the enemy with the wave of a hand..."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Leader.cfg:47
msgid "soul-pierce"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Monk, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Monk.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Monk"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Monk, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Monk.cfg:28
msgid ""
"The followers continue to study magic and the glyphs carved into stone by the"
" Primevals long ago. Most of the glyphs' meaning is obscure, and the "
"Primevals don't appear interested in explaining anything, but this makes the "
"Monks work harder than ever to be deemed worthy."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Prior, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Prior.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Prior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Prior, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Prior.cfg:30
msgid ""
"The hardiest and most clever of the glyph readers extract the most knowledge,"
" and gain great attack power to bring glory to their sect."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=fire, range=melee
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Prior.cfg:40
msgid "staff flare"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Shield_High, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Shield-High.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Sun-Shield"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Shield_High, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Shield-High.cfg:23
msgid ""
"These fighters play a supporting role, stoically absorbing damage so that "
"their more hot tempered commrads survive long enough to accomplish their "
"goals. Their armour disipates heat and cold and energy blasts, so they have "
"higher than average resistance to fire, cold, and arcane damage."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Shield, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Shield.cfg:5
msgid "Primevalist Brightshield"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primevalist Shield, race=primevalist_human
#: ./units/primeval/Primevalist_Shield.cfg:21
msgid ""
"These fighters play a supporting role, stoically absorbing damage so that "
"their more hot tempered comrades survive long enough to accomplish their "
"goals. Their armour is designed to disipate heat and cold and energy blasts, "
"so they have higher than average resistance to fire, cold, and arcane damage."
"  They can form a very effective defensive line, but they are not expected to"
" make a good strike force."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Swiftfoot, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Swift.cfg:5
msgid "Swiftfoot"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=Primeval Swiftfoot, race=primeval, gender=female
#: ./units/primeval/Swift.cfg:21
msgid ""
"The Primeval Swiftfoots are a basic component of the Primeval forces, mostly "
"serving as scouts."
msgstr ""

