msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Zephyrist, race=south-seas_human, gender=female
#: ./units/south-seas/Caster_Zephyrist.cfg:5
msgid "female^Wind-Caller"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Zephyrist, race=south-seas_human, gender=female
#: ./units/south-seas/Caster_Zephyrist.cfg:22
msgid ""
"The Wind-Callers study the lore of the brighter gods. They pray for "
"favourable winds and a minimum of strife. They are successful at directing "
"wind-lashes, but the effort requires strength."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas GreaterAlbatross, race=gryphon, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Greater-Albatross.cfg:5
msgid "Greater Albatross"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Seaman, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman.cfg:5
msgid "Seaman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Seaman, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman.cfg:24
msgid ""
"The South-Seas Seamen are the core workers of the seafaring nation.  While "
"they don't have any particular combat skills, the life of a sailor is rough, "
"so they are tough enough to be useful."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman.cfg:31
msgid "oar"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas AbleSeaman, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman_Able-Seaman.cfg:5
msgid "Able-Seaman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas AbleSeaman, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman_Able-Seaman.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Though not Captains, Able-Seaman are higher ranking than the bulk of the "
"sailors and have more access to resources.  In these times of conflict, they "
"have melted some of the lead normally used for ballast and affixed it to the "
"end of a staff to create something similar to a hammer."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas DeckMaster, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman_Deck-Master.cfg:5
msgid "Deck-Master"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas DeckMaster, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman_Deck-Master.cfg:24
msgid ""
"Because they are not wealthy, Deck-Masters will never own a ship of any size,"
" but they are trusted on the larger vessals to keep the rest of the men in "
"line.  They have upgraded their pole-arm to an actual hammer, as much for the"
" appearance as any utility.  They also use a large hook to trap and restrict "
"enemy limbs and weapons."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=melee
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman_Deck-Master.cfg:47
msgid "hook"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Whirlwind, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman_Whirlwind.cfg:5
msgid "Whirl Wind"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Whirlwind, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Seaman_Whirlwind.cfg:24
msgid ""
"The Whirlwinds are specialists at damaging the sails and riggings of opponent"
" ships, they are sent to board vessals that are not yet secured.  They are "
"afforded much respect, and they enjoy a good life on shore, but their "
"profession generally ensures that it is a short life."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Shoreman, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman.cfg:5
msgid "Shoreman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Shoreman, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman.cfg:23
msgid ""
"The Shoremen are responsible for loading ships and breaking down retired "
"vessals to reclaim the components.  Almost all of this work involves ropes, "
"so the Shoremen are very skilled with this simple tool and can tie down even "
"moving animals.  A spike is very helpful in making splices, as well as "
"killing rats."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=impact, range=melee
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman.cfg:39
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman_Salvager.cfg:41
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman_Wrecker.cfg:44
msgid "rope"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Rover, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman_Rover.cfg:5
msgid "Sea Rover"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type], id=SouthSeas Rover, race=south-seas_human, gender=male
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman_Rover.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Some of the southern city-states earn their wealth through plunder and "
"exploitation. The roving pirates are not the strongest fighters, but they are"
" verstile enough to give trouble to almost any foe."
msgstr ""

#. [attack], type=pierce, range=ranged
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman_Rover.cfg:39
#: ./units/south-seas/Shoreman_Wolf.cfg:42
